  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening laboratory systems and pathogen surveillance in the Indo-Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment will support strengthening public health and clinical laboratory systems, pathogen surveillance and antimicrobial resistance solutions across the Indo-Pacific region. The investment includes a development grant supporting a strategic partnership with the Peter Doherty Institute for Infection and Immunity. The funded projects within this investment emphasise health system strengthening, One Health adoption, climate change adaptation, and gender, disability and social inclusion (GEDSI) integration for regional health security. The investment funds programs of work within: Cambodia, Fiji, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Papua New Guinea, Philippines, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Thailand, Timor-Leste and Vanuatu.</narrative>
  </description>
